  <process id="proc_refutation" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>pm:Stack of `refutation`. This document shows how the stack's layers and operations connect, and none of its figures. How much of the system the stack holds is stated on the laneSet. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/pools.sqlc]</documentation>
    <laneSet id="lanes_refutation" name="draw">
      <documentation>scope: unbounded. `complete` says there are no other layers of this system, `scoped` says somebody established what lies outside and left it out, `unbounded` says nobody looked. A lane set has no way to say which, so this sentence is the only place it is said. The filing's reason: the three layers this filing needs: the two the coupling observation runs between, and one bought continuously with no nameplate. What else exists was not the question this filing put [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</documentation>
      <documentation>coupling search: stated. `unmeasured` means nobody looked, `none` means somebody looked and found no dependence, `notApplicable` means there is no pair to couple, and `stated` means the dependences drawn here. An absent line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</documentation>
      <lane id="lane_refutation_compute" name="compute">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
      </lane>
      <lane id="lane_refutation_labour" name="labour">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
      </lane>
      <lane id="lane_refutation_object-storage" name="object-storage">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <textAnnotation id="note_refutation_dependence">
      <text>A dotted arrow between two lanes is a dependence somebody observed: not a supply edge, and never evidence for a fusion. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/dependences.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_refutation_lane">
      <text>An empty lane is a layer nothing draws on, not an idle one: every layer carries figures, and BPMN has no glyph to show them. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/lane_grain.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_refutation_scope">
      <text>Scope: unbounded. The pool is the whole system only when the filing says `complete`. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_refutation_search">
      <text>Coupling search: stated. An absent dependence line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="dep_refutation_compute_labour" sourceRef="tns:lane_refutation_compute" targetRef="tns:lane_refutation_labour" associationDirection="One">
      <documentation>an observed dependence: relieving `compute` moved `labour`. It is not a supply edge, and never evidence for a fusion. What was observed, and how strongly, is not in this document. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/dependences.sqlc]</documentation>
    </association>
